---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'; import {pillars,findings,principles,refs} from '../data/content.js';
---
<Base>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="mast"><div class="wrap identity"><div class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><b>AU</b></div><div><div class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT PUBLIC INTEREST REVIEW</div><div class="agency">Australian Digital Regulation Review</div><div class="subagency">Freedom • Innovation • Enterprise • Accountable Government</div></div></div></header>
<nav><div class="wrap nav"><a href="#review">The review</a><a href="#bill">Online safety</a><a href="#system">Regulatory system</a><a href="#reform">Reform agenda</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></div></nav>
<main id="main">
<section class="hero" id="review"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow gold">PUBLIC INTEREST PAPER • NOVEMBER 2026</div><h1>Safer online.<br><span>Freer by design.</span></h1><p class="lead">Australia can protect children and citizens from genuine digital harm without building a regulatory state that depends on ever broader access, duplicated compliance and blind trust in government.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#bill">Explore the findings</a><a class="textlink" href="#sources">Read primary sources →</a></div></div><aside class="brief"><div>THE CENTRAL TEST</div><blockquote>Would we still grant this power if it were exercised by the government we trust least?</blockquote><p>Good institutions do not require perfect officials. They remain trustworthy when people are mistaken, compromised, politically motivated or corrupt.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap pillars">{pillars.map(([h,p])=><article><h3>{h}</h3><p>{p}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="bill"><div class="kicker">01 • THE TRIGGER</div><h2>The Online Safety Amendment deserves serious scrutiny</h2><p class="intro">The bill has legitimate safety objectives, but it materially expands the architecture around platform risk assessment, mitigation and regulatory enforcement. The issue is not whether online harm exists. It is whether the powers, incentives and information flows are proportionate and safely constrained.</p><div class="fact"><b>Status</b><span>Before the Senate. Senate committee report due 20 November 2026.</span><a href={refs[1][2]}>Parliamentary record →</a></div><div class="cards">{findings.slice(0,3).map(([h,f,a])=><article><span class="num">FINDING</span><h3>{h}</h3><p>{f}</p><hr><strong>Review position</strong><p>{a}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="dark" id="system"><div class="wrap section"><div class="kicker pale">02 • THE SYSTEM</div><h2>One power is not the whole picture</h2><p class="intro pale">Privacy, online safety, AI, digital identity, cyber security, telecommunications, financial regulation and national security increasingly act on the same people, systems and evidence.</p><div class="system-grid"><div class="stack"><span>ONLINE SAFETY</span><span>PRIVACY</span><span>AI GOVERNANCE</span><span>CYBER / SOCI</span><span>DIGITAL IDENTITY</span><span>SURVEILLANCE</span></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="citizen"><b>CITIZEN<br>& BUSINESS</b><small>Repeated obligations<br>Connected datasets<br>Higher compliance cost<br>Growing state capability</small></div></div><div class="cards darkcards">{findings.slice(3).map(([h,f,a])=><article><h3>{h}</h3><p>{f}</p><strong>Approach</strong><p>{a}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="reform"><div class="kicker">03 • THE ALTERNATIVE</div><h2>Consolidate administration. Distribute power. Strengthen review.</h2><p class="intro">Government should feel integrated to the citizen without the citizen becoming fully visible to government.</p><div class="principles">{principles.map((p,i)=><div><b>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</b><span>{p}</span></div>)}</div><div class="architecture"><h3>Privacy-preserving government architecture</h3><div class="flow"><div>Authorised case<br><small>purpose + legislation</small></div><i>→</i><div>Policy gateway<br><small>least privilege</small></div><i>→</i><div>Federated source<br><small>ATO / health / identity</small></div><i>→</i><div>Minimum answer<br><small>yes/no/attribute</small></div><i>→</i><div>Immutable audit<br><small>independent review</small></div></div></div></section>
<section class="service"><div class="wrap section"><div class="kicker">04 • PUBLIC SERVICE</div><h2>Authority is a responsibility to serve, not a privilege to command.</h2><div class="columns"><div><h3>Citizen-first administration</h3><p>One front door, plain-language requirements, assistance before punitive enforcement for honest mistakes, published service levels and meaningful reasons for consequential decisions.</p></div><div><h3>Review as a right</h3><p>Human reconsideration, accessible Ombudsman review, merits review where appropriate and judicial review must not depend on the original decision-maker deciding that scrutiny is warranted.</p></div><div><h3>Worst-case engineering</h3><p>Use separation of duties, time-bound authority, independent approval, immutable logs, anomaly detection, data minimisation and statutory deletion.</p></div></div></section></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="sources"><div class="kicker">05 • EVIDENCE</div><h2>Primary sources</h2><p class="intro">This review is independent commentary. It is not an Australian Government publication. Claims should be tested against primary legislation, parliamentary material and regulator publications.</p><div class="sources">{refs.map(([org,title,url],i)=><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><b>{org}</b><p>{title}</p></div><i>↗</i></a>)}</div></section>
</main><footer><div class="wrap"><strong>Australian Digital Regulation Review</strong><p>Independent public-interest analysis • Not affiliated with or endorsed by the Australian Government.</p><p class="legal">Branding note: this site intentionally does not reproduce the Commonwealth Coat of Arms. PM&C states that the Arms signify Commonwealth authority and ownership, and third-party use may require written permission.</p></div></footer>
</Base>
